<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46168" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζευγίτης</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῑ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ</span>,
		fem. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζευγῖτις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ιδος</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζεῦγος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>yoked in pairs</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζευγίτιδες ἵπποι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					48
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμίονοι ζευγῖται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					17.71
				</span></i>
			; of soldiers, <i>in the same rank</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Pel.</u>
				23
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάλαμος ζ</span>. a reed <i>of
				which were made the mouthpieces of the double flutes</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζεύγη</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				4.11.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζευγῖται, οἱ</span>, the third of Solon's four classes of Athenian
			citizens, so called from <i>their being able to keep a team</i>
				(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζεῦγος</span>) <i>of oxen</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1274a20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ath.</u>
				4.3
			</span></i>, Lexap.<i><span class="en">
				D.
				43.54
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12.45.40
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
